#>plan_ecosystem_architecture_wip
#:operation #!cache
#:fixity #!tending
#:layer #!pragmatics

@plan: ~"./PLAN.md"
@index: ~"./index.spw"
@wip_notebook: ~"../../../.spw/conventions/wip-notebook.spw"
@peer_kit_script: ~"../../../scripts/build-peer-kit.mjs"
@expression_manifest: ~"../../../scripts/build-expression-manifest.mjs"
@expression_resonance: ~"../../../public/js/runtime/expression/expression-resonance.js"
@operator_detection: ~"../../../public/js/kernel/operator-detection.js"
@css_bundle: ~"../../../scripts/ts/css-bundle.mts"
@spw_quest: ~"../spw-quest/PLAN.md"

operation = "cache"
fixity = "tending"

^"stream"{
 >>[2026-10-25 17:10] verify — Read the CSS, the runtime and spw.quest against their owner plans. The plan ranks eight site slices by what they are worth to peers, adoption, the codebase as an asset, and risk; spw.quest gains G, H and I. Two findings had no owner. 195 KB of the 338 KB expression manifest (SPW_PROJECTION_SEEDS, 33 KB gzip) loads wherever a page carries an expression, and getProjectionSeeds() has no caller. Three services route bundles are byte-identical.
 >>[2026-10-25 17:21] verify — The parser equivalence probe: spw-workbench-reader.js parse and spw-workbench-parser.js parse agree on success, completeness, AST, tokens, errors, warnings and events for 990 of 990 git-tracked .spw files outside the workbench, once duration and event timestamps are left out. S3 loses its gate.
 >>[2026-10-25 20:34] implement — S0: each owner plan keeps its dated figure and gains today's beside it (catalog 146; site.js 52.6 KB; flips 366, home 70, about 45, play 25; core 1721 of 1741 KiB; 184 of 188 sheets with a banner; pin 0eb1d1c0; two engages defs). Layer order is named at style-core.css:1 in readability and css-instruction.spw. runtime-plane-consolidation names both seams: expression-query reads slots and geometry reads layout (proposed, unowned), and per-pass recalc stays with runtime-bootstrap-performance. spw-quest's What it is now is re-measured and slice B is marked done.
 >>[2026-10-25 20:39] implement — S1, the second option: the seeds leave the build until a reader asks, and getProjectionSeeds goes with its only write. spw-expressions.js 340,216 → 143,521 B, 63.3 → 30.7 KB gzip. The harvest read the .spw canon only for the seeds, so the expression stamp now counts routes and its harvester; a .spw edit no longer forces a manifest rebuild in any session. test:modules 702 pass; check:built 145 of 145 on a fresh build.
 >>[2026-10-25 20:43] implement — S6: services-surface holds routes/surfaces/services.css alone, and services-creator, -ecosystem and -systems alias to it in ROUTE_SURFACE_ALIASES. The new bundle has the md5 the three shared; the rendered pages link it, services-care keeps its own, and css-bundle-filter gains the alias test (18 pass).
 >>[2026-10-25 20:50] implement — S2: operator-info, the profile builder, shared.js (threshold, composite, prefix regex) and the geometry scanner read operator names from operator-detection.js. A before-and-after dump of every table is identical but for $ and meta (meta → substrate), % (label normalization) and 30 canon aliases now resolving, substrate among them. The boonhonk mixer's five rows are charges with a printed glyph and stay. operator-views.test.mjs 4 pass; test:modules 707; build:peer-kit --check current; check:workers green.
 >>[2026-10-25 21:02] implement — S3: the reader gives the parser's parse on 993 of 993 tracked .spw files and its parseExpression on 974 of 974 route expressions (probe re-run with timing fields left out). spw-paste, spw-document-project, spw-runtime-parser, site.js's build line, four tests and the quest's reader, build and file-reader import the reader; build:spw-parser cuts one bundle, byte-identical to the reader before; carry-parser carries it, so the quest's /parser.js is 87,530 B where it was 75,779. The 75.8 KB parser bundle is deleted. test:modules 706; quest tests 52; check:built 145; check:local green.
 >>[2026-10-25 21:20] implement — G on the local branch quest/specimens (a4d6c3ea), off main so the note deploys without it: /specimens, a slot search over 1019 specimens, and ground then edge for two lines; see that branch's spw-quest stream. Receipt for spw-language-v04: expression-query's slot reader takes nine herbarium forms only in part (nested bodies, three-way joins, ; lists, chained capsules) and every route line whole.
 >>[2026-10-27 13:32] probe — wonder_ecosystem_what_travels: the list already exists. scripts/build-peer-kit.mjs keeps SCRIPTS by worker (one entry, pinch-text-scale for spw-quest) and writes PEER_SCRIPTS with peerScriptPath; nothing under public/ marks what travels. Run before any ~#expect was on record, so it measures and tests nothing.
 >>[2026-10-27 13:32] probe — wonder_ecosystem_specimen_host: public/js defines no custom element; the two hits are workers/factshift-center's own app. A specimen host would be the runtime's first. Run before any ~#expect was on record.
}

^"s0_rows"{  # owner plan text the tree no longer matches, measured 2026-10-25
 catalog_defs = "146 live defs (core 4, feature 49, region 1, enhancement 92); runtime-plane-consolidation cites 96, module-contract-overhaul 114, deploy-module-graph 105"
 bundle_note = "runtime-plane-consolidation says no bundle step; deploy-module-graph shipped the packs (f05b02d2)"
 bootstrap_baseline = "runtime-bootstrap-performance cites site.js at 121 KB and site-settings.js at 102 KB; today 52.6 KB and a 659 B barrel"
 layer_order_home = "css-architecture-readability and css-instruction.spw import_manifest say style.css declares the layer order; it is public/css/style-core.css:1"
 flip_counts = "css-cascade-stratification cites 365 flips (home 71, about 43); audit:layer-flip gives 363 (home 67, about 45)"
 ecology_figures = "stylesheet-ecology.spw cites 1595 of 1638 KiB core, tokens/core.css about 91 KiB, and 151 of 155 sheets; today 1721 of 1741 KiB, 103 KiB, and 188 source files; metaphysical-paper.css already idle-loads"
 workbench_pin = "spw-language-v04 cites 229aedcf; the mount and both generated parsers are at 0eb1d1c0"
 browser_parser = "interaction-grammar puts a browser-side Spw parser out of scope; the site has shipped one since Phase 4 of spw-language-v04"
 engages = "engagement-clusters cites 3 engages fields; the catalog has 2"
 quest_now = "spw-quest What it is now (measured 2026-10-12) lacks /read, /parser/ releases and /script.spw"
 expression_reader = "runtime-plane-consolidation Phase 4 names spw-expression-geometry.js the one reader; spw-language-v04 extends expression-query.js"
 recalc_owner = "core-css-spend-cut hands recalc to runtime-bootstrap-performance; runtime-plane-consolidation Phase 7 claims core CSS decomposition"
}

^"probes"{
 seeds_reader = `rg -n "getProjectionSeeds" --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/_workbench/**' --glob '!dist/**' .`
 parser_equivalence = `import both bundles from public/js/semantic/, parse every git-tracked .spw outside the workbench, and compare the results with duration left out`
 services_bundles = `md5 public/css/bundles/routes/services-*.css`
 layer_flip = `npm run -s audit:layer-flip`
}

^"open"{
 what_travels = ~"./index.spw#wonder_ecosystem_what_travels"
 specimen_host = ~"./index.spw#wonder_ecosystem_specimen_host"
 first_portable = "site-starter-component-kit's wonder: a capability or the design specimen. This plan proposes a third answer, the Spw instrument, because spw.quest already consumes the peer kit. The creator's call."
 arrival_lever = "runtime-plane-consolidation's wonder: route family or engagement. ctx.routeFamily is computed and unread. The creator's call."
 quest_motion = ~"../spw-quest/index.spw#wonder_spw_quest_motion"
}
